set heading(numbering: none)

`small` · magnify · a smaller version, about four fifths.

# Form

`x.small` on a symbol, `(a + b).small` on a group. A recipe has one base and up to three operations.

# Examples

| Recipe | Result | Glyph |
|:--|:-:|:--|
| `T.up.small` | $T.up.small$ | built and cached |
| `x.small` | $x.small$ | built and cached |

# Four layers

| Layer | For this operation |
|:--|:--|
| Meaning | A smaller version, about four fifths. A guideline, not a rule. |
| Style | Use a `sym` to give a recipe a short name. |
| Construction | A smaller or larger copy of the base. |
| Glyph | The font glyph when the font has one, otherwise a built glyph kept in the recipe cache. |

# Rules

- More than three operations on one base gives a warning.
- Scales the base to four fifths of its size.

# From LaTeX

no direct LaTeX command.

